  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nCampaign durations are supposed to align to hourly epochs, but _createCampaign only enforces duration >= HOUR and never checks duration % HOUR == 0 (see DistributionCreator.sol#L247-L287). An operator can create a campaign with a duration like HOUR + 1, which passes all on-chain checks and pulls the creator’s funds into the Distributor. The off-chain engine expects integer-hour epochs; a non–hour-multiple is likely rejected or ignored, so no Merkle root is ever produced for this campaign. Result: the creator’s reward tokens are stranded in the Distributor with no on-chain recovery path (except governor sweep), violating the “campaign pre-deposit protection” and “creator autonomy” assumptions.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nIn _createCampaign, enforce alignment to the epoch duration, e.g., require(newCampaign.duration % HOUR == 0, Errors.InvalidParam());. Optionally also enforce startTimestamp % HOUR == 0 if the engine requires start-time alignment. Reject any campaign with a non-hour-multiple duration before pulling funds.",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Test file\n\ntest/c4/C4PoCNonHourDuration.t.sol\n\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\n    import { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\n    import { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\n\n    /// PoC: duration not multiple of 1 hour is accepted, funds pulled to Distributor\n    contract C4PoCNonHourDuration is Fixture {\n      function setUp() public override {\n          super.setUp();\n\n          vm.prank(governor);\n          creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n          vm.startPrank(guardian);\n          address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n          uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n          tokens[0] = address(angle);\n          amounts[0] = 1e8;\n          creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n          vm.stopPrank();\n\n          angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n          vm.prank(alice);\n          angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n      }\n\n      function test_submissionValidity() external {\n          uint256 amount = 5e8;            // above min-per-epoch\n          uint32 duration = EPOCH_DURATION + 1; // violates hour multiple\n          uint32 futureStart = uint32(block.timestamp + EPOCH_DURATION);\n\n          uint256 bobBalanceBefore = angle.balanceOf(bob);\n          vm.prank(alice);\n          bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(\n              CampaignParameters({\n                  campaignId: bytes32(0),\n                  creator: alice,\n                  rewardToken: address(angle),\n                  amount: amount,\n                  campaignType: 1,\n                  startTimestamp: futureStart,\n                  duration: duration,\n                  campaignData: bytes(\"non_hour\")\n              })\n          );\n\n          // Confirm non-hour duration stored and funds pulled\n          CampaignParameters memory campaign = creator.campaign(campaignId);\n          assertEq(campaign.duration, duration, \"duration not stored\");\n          uint256 expectedNet = (amount * (1e9 - creator.defaultFees())) / 1e9;\n          assertEq(angle.balanceOf(bob) - bobBalanceBefore, expectedNet, \"funds not pulled\");\n      }\n    }\n\n### How to run\n\nforge test --match-test submissionValidity --match-path test/c4/C4PoCNonHourDuration.t.sol\n\nExpected: Test passes, showing a non-hour duration is accepted and still pulls the creator’s funds.",
